Answer: When attributes are given values inside the class, every newly created object initially receives those values. Example:

```java
class Bird {
String name = "Parakeet";
String family = "Parrot";
int age = 2;
int cost = 7000;
}
```

When a Bird object is created, it initially contains: Name → Parakeet Family → Parrot Age → 2 Cost → 7000

Answer: Yes. The default values can be used as they are, or they can be changed after creating the object.

```java
Bird bird2 = new Bird();
bird2.name = "Parity";
bird2.family = "African Parrot";
bird2.age = 3;
bird2.cost = 30000;
```

The new values replace the previous values in bird2.

