Answer: ```java
Bird bird1 = new Bird();
Bird bird2 = new Bird();
bird1.fly();
bird1.makeSound();
bird2.fly();
bird2.makeSound();
new Bird().fly();
new Bird().makeSound();
```

Four objects are created. Objects with references → 2 Objects without references → 2 The first object is referred to by bird1. The second object is referred to by bird2.

```java
new Bird().fly() creates one anonymous object.
new Bird().makeSound() creates another anonymous object.
```

Each use of new Bird() creates a separate object.

