Explanation num1 and num2 have default values 10 and 20. casioCalci changes the values to 200 and 100. All behaviours are called using casioCalci. citizenCalci uses the default values.

```java
new Calculator().average() creates an anonymous calculator object.
```

The anonymous object invokes average() only once.

